Reference travel plugin inspected read-only:
/Users/mac/code/ide/NovaIsland-Tech/Nova-Travel-Marketing-dashboard/plugin-src/src/lib/hooks-table.mjs
SessionStart=10s; UserPromptSubmit/Stop/StopFailure=5s; Codex Interrupt=3s.
Its run-node first selects WORKBUDDY_EXTRA_PATHS Node, then PATH or other installed Node; it does not cold-start a newly copied pinned Node or hash that binary every invocation.
Its turn hook reads stdin synchronously; actual WorkBuddy HookExecutor closes stdin. Nova Content Hub already bounds its input read at 600ms.
Therefore the reference 5s measurement (0.1-0.3s warm) is not a cold-runtime budget measurement for this product.

Disposition:
No blind hook timeout increase or validation removal is justified. Warm CLI passes do not prove native WorkBuddy generation; parent agent owns native UI retry of the same unchanged handoff.
If product prevention is requested: preserve metadata-only Skill discovery; separately validate the exact installed executable/launcher/release hashes and await a read-only runtime probe before handoff creation/opening, shared by cover and template launches. Do not execute an unverified cache root from installedAssistantSkill, which currently verifies release and Skill bytes but not executable/launcher hashes. Do not warm an app-bundled copy when the host will execute a different installed cache inode.
Uncovered: a new fully cold native WorkBuddy installation retry; deterministic >5000ms reproduction; production/provider generation acceptance.
